{"title":"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Compute the largest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5d23b6f717ba85ee1a4ae7a094310f9002d7c5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2004^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c47d07b2d07f9731fb8a26ed5472d07cfc1487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2004!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a real number with the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/3/683bf6f16134ed7ec2d5f139dc46838cad44dd21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+\\tfrac1x = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"77\" height=\"21\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/6/7c6d63c1ee840e2960b8e34356c880fa7059cd84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_m = x^m + \\tfrac{1}{x^m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"21\" />. Determine the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b29699446f0faca3d3e99da1ee5cf1ec0ca70aa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a box, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> green balls, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blue balls, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red balls, a brown ball, a white ball, and a black ball. These balls are randomly drawn out of the box one at a time (without replacement) until two of the same color have been removed. This process requires that at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> balls be removed. The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> balls are drawn can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eeca0ea912b8efe0468a9a5dc06a2fc8a2e45c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{5^k | k \\in \\textbf{Z}, 0 \\le k \\le 2004 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"231\" height=\"20\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/2758fc952d5bff448f24097070fab5f288d371db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{2004} = 5443 \\cdots 0625$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"160\" height=\"15\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d1f265f87c2649f0c2722efc85558c071c55fc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1401$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> digits, how many elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> begin with the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />? \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25619b168b13802d30603e0b394037b2b0a2be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac1n = 0.d_1d_2d_3d_4\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"141\" height=\"21\" />, an infinite decimal that has the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245551e06664fe19f066db1c096c6b8efbb1a5c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i = d_{i+12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e61ce09efe3f712dc81b4013adc833fb23dbb813.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9901$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is prime, how many positive integers are in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />? (The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1544d77330dc5a289ad6a42beeb236b8dd70a9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> are digits.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a scalene triangle. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are selected on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. The cevians <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> concur at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d93a1bd2d2dcfeb38669318a052bf729fc4a0589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AFP] = 126$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aed67d948747fc766805ef9297d0350a550f1970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[FBP] = 63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/924f1128499e5e5f9c6dfa6a874a1d52c2e0bae1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[CEP] = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, determine the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Anders, Po-Ru, Reid, and Aaron are playing Bridge. After one hand, they notice that all of the cards of the two suits are split between Reid and Po-Ru's hands. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> denote the number of ways <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cards can be dealt to each player such that this is the case. Determine the remainder obtained when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. (Bridge is a game played with the standard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-card deck.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the remainder obtained when the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/2432b88bdbb249cbe5572b81ede9d2403dc9cb3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2004^{2003^{2002^{2001}}}\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"22\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/642a3134837deae29f73ef1e2df3daa87321b4e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1+x^3)\\left(1+2x^{3^2}\\right)\\cdots \\left(1+kx^{3^k}\\right) \\cdots \\left(1+1997x^{3^{1997}}\\right) = 1+a_1 x^{k_1} + a_2 x^{k_2} + \\cdots + a_m x^{k_m}\\]\" width=\"659\" height=\"32\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c722bdd55a0cb1c177c8bf7269d47b62cd94da1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1eb239ac02729483468bf9d79708b9b1db6d21f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1 &lt; k_2 &lt; \\cdots &lt; k_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"15\" />. Determine the remainder obtained when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01cf8f4cf8d0916ff1f466f213c12473453a36d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> is a cyclic pentagon with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7abe4deafa7d65ecd5721f7ab789b7354005acca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = CD = DE$\" width=\"137\" height=\"12\" />. The diagonals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e064fcde9dc4ccefa123647537b77b0e825ae87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA = 25$\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/707ee619459430f2a1abf044ef12b9acb70d98ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD = 113$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374f57f56338e0ad3212ed5a5b5fad7c97b8992b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" />. The area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Determine the remainder obtained when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/2/75212ff6ab19289ae214e99f1f22526e34f9023f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x-200)(4x+1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e561d8bca3fd8b55b65c1b7f6d1f2cb0d911d996.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\omega = \\tan^{-1}(\\alpha) + \\tan^{-1}(\\beta) + \\tan^{-1} (\\gamma).\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"19\" /> The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fa0a0e873426976a635b5ace19eef7a3b2c5b91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\omega)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Determine the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd4babab25c9e82e2e8c30b21a070981213d4a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95c180b12878c1f359607e0af47b48fcf4950d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/81729cf4848260b6feda8ea5ae3f1d0867c890eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e43ab3616df7169cf742ede9da39ff3dc2ef38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA = 7$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> denote the circumcenter and intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f254a6e559e5211c72e633c720ad5ca6cc8c6a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP^2$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Determine the remainder obtained when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is a polynomial of minimal degree that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/796ffd1dab4b44ff4e70c2b4709028da0bf7763b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(k) = \\dfrac{1}{k(k+1)}\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"41\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/589bb8c642e4f8d967809caf8bcb1462e2731aa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1, 2, 3, \\ldots, 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" />. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/9/20971d06479da16fa586686dc7a948c359d8d64c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(11)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae8e7a16882e8e7844d5654bf54ce9aa3ef4df3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> Elm trees, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> Dogwood trees, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> Oak trees are to be planted in a line in front of a library such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/6/9b6d8951c02eea2af505df6f4c0011714f6edf60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} i&amp;) \\text{ No two Elm trees are next to each other.} \\\\ ii&amp;) \\text{ No Dogwood tree is adjacent to an Oak tree.} \\\\ iii&amp;) \\text{ All of the trees are planted.} \\end{align*}\" width=\"357\" height=\"68\" /> How many ways can the trees be situated in this manner?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/7432aa0296ea3db0e1f9dad049071ef0ad881f8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/6/716417cd0c2bac7416d80fff1c68f671d466d018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA = 37$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f77a691c511984c239482fb3480829d7043af14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are selected on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> concur at the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/27276f9d140507f24de0cc397161ceaec09a98c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{AD} + \\dfrac{1}{BE} + \\dfrac{1}{CF}\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"37\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018100129\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 665/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest e